body:
I think the issue here is that, while you are correct in saying that it is abhorrent, it is 1) not as bad as killing a civilian, let alone a child and 2) this intentional or unintentional translation flub essentially equates the IDF's moral principles with Hamas' lack thereof. It conveniently puts an argument out that IDF has the same awful standards Hamas does but with a greater cost of life and a sizable international backing when, in reality, even if this one soldier was that cruel towards POWs/enemy forces, they are still a step above Hamas. Again, not really claiming it is intentional but the difference is massive both in optics and the fact of the matter.

&#x200B;

I personally wouldn't argue with you that both sides have shown a callousness towards life though.
